{#
    The top of an error page: its code, a title and an explanation, then whatever leads the visitor on (a search,
    buttons), and a way to reach us. Beside it on a computer, the drawing of the error ("illustration", a name of
    <twig:Illustration>), hidden below the lg breakpoint.

    <twig:ErrorPage code="404" illustration="not-found" label="Page introuvable" title="Cette page n'existe pas" description="…" />

    Composed:
    <twig:ErrorPage code="404" illustration="not-found" label="Page introuvable" icon="lucide:compass">
        <twig:ErrorPage:Title>Cette page n'existe pas</twig:ErrorPage:Title>
        <twig:ErrorPage:Description>…</twig:ErrorPage:Description>
        <twig:ErrorPage:Search city="toulouse" />
        <twig:ErrorPage:Actions>
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="…">…</a>
        </twig:ErrorPage:Actions>
    </twig:ErrorPage>
#}
{% props code, illustration, label = null, icon = 'lucide:compass', title = null, description = null, contact = true %}
<section {{ attributes.defaults({class: 'hero-glow error-hero py-5'}) }}>
    <div class="container-lg">
        <div class="row g-4 g-lg-5 align-items-center">
            <div class="col-lg-7">
                <twig:ErrorPage:Code code="{{ code }}" label="{{ label }}" icon="{{ icon }}" />
                {% block content %}
                    {% if title %}<twig:ErrorPage:Title>{{ title }}</twig:ErrorPage:Title>{% endif %}
                    {% if description %}<twig:ErrorPage:Description>{{ description }}</twig:ErrorPage:Description>{% endif %}
                {% endblock %}
                {% if contact %}<twig:ErrorPage:Contact />{% endif %}
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-5 d-none d-lg-block text-center">
                <twig:Illustration name="{{ illustration }}" width="{{ 360 }}" priority="{{ true }}" />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
